With Courier New, the smallest readable font size is 8pt (it's really 7,
but you get eye strain.)  There are 10 pixels per line with that font. 

In the modern computer, the highest resultion you can see normally would be
1600x1200 - it can be higher, but those aren't common on a desktop.  The
result is that there are a maximum of 120 lines on the screen, thus
cut-n-paste the following:

****** SPOILER SPACE ****** SPOILER SPACE ****** SPOILER SPACE ******

****** SPOILER SPACE ****** SPOILER SPACE ****** SPOILER SPACE ******

... and so on until 120 lines have been reached.    It may take more
bandwidth, but the obvious and large notice will prevent any complaint. ;)

Granted, it's possible to have higher resolutions.  However, the people
working on those stations either don't read nethack newsgroups on that
screen, or have probably looked through the source enough to be spoiled
already.  Thus, complaints from those people should be minimal at best.



